origin: BCI_paper (archived in /media/amir/Arxive/BCI_paper), commit cc819ec (2026-10-13); made 2026-11-03 as a smaller
replacement for the lmem2g validation design (the 64-neuron latch core, which did not route with LibreLane: 30 %
stopped after 27 h at 209 796 violations, 20 % still in global routing after 36 h; the owner agreed to a smaller core;
lmem2g's files are in git at commit 37c170b, validation/designs/lmem2g).
The project never hardened this variant, so there is no project result to compare with.
  rtl/bmi_snn_lmem16.v          <- generated by gen_rtl.py (this directory) from rtl/bmi_snn_par.v (last commit 1aca256):
                                   the logic of sw/gen_variant.py with bmi_snn_lmem2g's entry (HARDWIRED 0, V_BITS 20,
                                   O_BITS 24, DENSE 1; LATCH_MEM, GATE_DP, W2_PIPE) and H = 16 instead of 64. For H = 64 the
                                   script reproduces lmem2g's rtl/bmi_snn_lmem2g.v byte for byte. The memory map is the
                                   same (row c at words 16c .. 16c+3, W2 at 1600+j); 97 + 16 row clock gates.
  tb/tb_bmi_snn.v               <- sim/tb_bmi_snn.v (last commit 1aca256), unchanged (identical to lmem2g's)
  stim/weights.hex, stats.json  <- sim/vecfull_h16_indy_20160630_01/ (git-ignored vector set of the 16-neuron cores,
                                   generated 2026-09-19; weights in the same 2048-word memory map, unused words zero)
  stim/stream_w50.hex           <- sim/vecfull_h16_indy_20160630_01/stream.hex, cut after the 50th tick (`awk '{print}
                                   /^ff$/{n++; if(n==50) exit}'`): the first 50 bins, 206 tokens (156 events + 50 ticks),
                                   the same events as the min32_asap7 design's stimulus
  stim/expect_w50.hex           <- sim/vecfull_h16_indy_20160630_01/expect.hex, first 100 lines (y0, y1 of 50 bins)
  The vectors were made for the 16-neuron cores with 16-bit state (bmi_snn_min16); this variant keeps lmem2g's 20/24-bit
  state, which gives the same outputs here: the RTL simulation is bit-exact on all 50 bins with 0 real-time overruns
  (flow/rtl_sim.sh, 2026-11-03).
  sdc/bmi_snn_lmem16.sdc        <- lmem2g's sdc/bmi_snn_lmem2g.sdc (latch waivers removed, derating / 100.0; it has no
                                   size-dependent line), header comment changed
  LibreLane settings (design.sh CONFIG_EXTRA): those of lmem2g, plus CTS_APPLY_NDR none (sky130 notes 5.1: designs with
  many gated clock nets; lmem2g's global router dropped the clock NDR on 725 nets to reduce congestion, GRT-0273).
  FIRM_CLOCK_GATES 1 (added 2026-11-03): the first run lost the clock input of one row clock gate in CTS at both
  utilisations (u_icg_j11 at 30 %, u_icg_r93 at 20 %; OpenROAD issue #9816, sky130 notes 9.2). With the gates fixed
  where global placement left them, hold failed by 0.36 and 0.49 ns (clock-wire detours); placed at the centre of
  their rows first, by 0.057 and 0.089 ns, at ff only (sky130 notes 5.1).
Testbench defines as for lmem2g, with N_BINS 50 and the stimulus above; SDF simulation (SIM_MODE sdf), which lmem2g's
size did not allow.
